      "title": "Democrats blast Trump’s decision to make Stephen Miller his chief of staff as president defends picking loyal ‘MVP’ - as it happened",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2026/nov/06/us-midterm-elections-2026-democrats-blue-wave-congress-latest-news-updates",
      "description": "<p>This live blog is now closed.</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/06/stephen-miller-chief-of-staff-trump\">Stephen Miller, architect of Trump’s immigration crackdown, to become White House chief of staff</a></p></li><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/news/2026/feb/17/sign-up-for-the-breaking-news-us-email-to-get-newsletter-alerts-direct-to-your-inbox?utm_medium=ACQUISITIONS_STANDFIRST&amp;utm_campaign=BN22326&amp;utm_content=signup&amp;utm_term=standfirst&amp;utm_source=GUARDIAN_WEB\">Sign up for Breaking News US email</a></p></li></ul><p><strong>Donald Trump will begin the day in Washington today. </strong></p><p>He has closed door meetings for much of the day, and will take part in a Diwali celebration at the White House at 1:30pm ET. While that’s currently not open to the press we’ll let you know if that opens up.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2026/nov/06/us-midterm-elections-2026-democrats-blue-wave-congress-latest-news-updates\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-07T03:02:26"
    },
    {
      "title": "Stephen Miller, architect of Trump’s immigration crackdown, to become White House chief of staff",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/06/stephen-miller-chief-of-staff-trump",
      "description": "<p>US president confirms Susie Wiles, current chief of staff and first woman to serve in the role, will step down</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2026/nov/06/us-midterm-elections-2026-democrats-blue-wave-congress-latest-news-updates\">US politics live – latest updates</a></p></li></ul><p>Stephen Miller, <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump\">Donald Trump</a>’s most controversial aide and the architect of his sweeping immigration crackdown, will become his new White House chief of staff days after Republicans lost control of the US Congress in US midterm elections.</p><p>The president announced the extraordinary appointment on Friday, confirming that <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/dec/25/trump-chief-of-staff-susie-wiles\">Susie Wiles</a> – his current chief of staff, and the first woman to serve in the role – had been ousted.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/06/stephen-miller-chief-of-staff-trump\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-07T01:38:06"
    },
    {
      "title": "How Stephen Miller appointment shows Trump hasn’t learned his lesson on immigration",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/06/donald-trump-stephen-miller-immigration",
      "description": "<p>US voters repudiated mass deportation campaign, but choice of new chief of staff shows Trump doesn’t care</p><p>On Tuesday, voters resoundingly rebuked Donald Trump and his brutal mass deportation campaign that sent military tanks and masked agents though residential streets.</p><p>But on Friday, the president doubled down. He named Stephen Miller – the architect of the administration’s most aggressive immigration policies – as his chief of staff.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/06/donald-trump-stephen-miller-immigration\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-07T01:04:52"
    },
    {
      "title": "Susie Wiles exits White House as Trump ousts another woman from key role",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/06/susie-wiles-white-house-resignation",
      "description": "<p>Wiles thanks president for ‘honor of a lifetime’ as departure leaves behind overwhelmingly male leadership team</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2026/nov/06/us-midterm-elections-2026-democrats-blue-wave-congress-latest-news-updates\">US politics live – latest updates</a></p></li></ul><p>Donald Trump on Friday said Susie Wiles, the first woman to serve as White House chief of staff, will leave her post, a major shake-up of his inner circle that comes amid a steady exodus of senior female officials from his administration.</p><p>The president <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/06/stephen-miller-chief-of-staff-trump\">announced</a> her ouster – and her replacement, by the immigration hardliner Stephen Miller – in a post on Truth Social, days after a <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/04/democrats-house-midterm-elections-results\">sweeping blue wave</a> gave Democrats control of both chambers of Congress in the midterm elections. Wiles’s departure leaves behind an overwhelmingly male leadership team.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/06/susie-wiles-white-house-resignation\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-06T22:35:09"
    },
